{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_implementation_plan", "label": "mlforge Invoice Implementation Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mlforge_invoice_product", "label": "mlforge Invoice Product", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "get_paid_faster_positioning", "label": "\"Get Paid Faster\" Positioning", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Audience-neutral positioning deliberately broadened beyond a freelancer wedge, since anyone who sends invoices and gets paid late (agencies, contractors, consultants, landlords, solo SaaS founders) shares the same problem \u2014 the freelancer framing was a wedge, not the ceiling."}, {"id": "reminder_engine_core_loop", "label": "Reminder Engine Core Loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "why_no_cloudflare_rationale", "label": "Why No Cloudflare Decision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Originally chose Cloudflare Workers for the reminder cron+queue, but two codebases and two deploy pipelines meant more places for state to drift, for a workload Vercel Cron + Next.js route handlers handle fine at this scale; fold-into-Next.js wins on operational simplicity until proven load or cost forces a split back out."}, {"id": "phase1_stripe_oauth_gap", "label": "Phase 1: Stripe OAuth Mock-Key Gap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/api/v1/stripe/callback currently stores a mock restricted key instead of exchanging the OAuth code at connect.stripe.com/oauth/token \u2014 the one piece standing between 'looks connected' and 'is actually connected', must be fixed before any real user touches Settings."}, {"id": "phase3_auto_pause_gap", "label": "Phase 3: Reminder Auto-Pause-on-Payment Gap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A reminder sequence currently only stops if a human pauses it; once the Stripe webhook lands it must mark sequences completed the moment an invoice flips to paid \u2014 flagged as the trust-critical bug, since a paid client still getting a Day 7 reminder breaks confidence immediately."}, {"id": "phase5_audience_pivot", "label": "Phase 5: Broaden Beyond Stripe-Only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Manual invoice tracking and a Mark-as-Paid override are required so anyone paid by bank transfer, check, or invoiced via QuickBooks/Xero (most small businesses) isn't locked out \u2014 this phase is what actually makes the 'not just freelancers' audience pivot real; don't market 'works for everyone' until it does."}, {"id": "stripe_connect_module", "label": "Stripe Read-Only Connect Module", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "stripe_callback_route", "label": "/api/v1/stripe/callback", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md", "source_